{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"OPERATOR-ATTESTED — THE PAIRED-RUN ParityReport. Both class slots MEASURED. Neither slot clears\nthe parity bar. The failing criterion in both cases is \"zero decision-level flips on the gold\nset\", and every flip is GENUINE, not the 635f artifact.\n\nRUN PROVENANCE\n  started  2026-08-02T22:29:38Z (standard) / 22:29:43Z (frontier)\n  finished 2026-08-03T00:07Z (standard) / 2026-08-02T23:49Z (frontier)\n  account 896586841071, region us-east-1, identity arn:aws:iam::896586841071:user/joe_frontier\n  code base: commit 4214516f95a (branch point). This PREDATES 48b3/77ed (sizing.py for an\n    unlocated primary) and the 8415/c403 overlap-token work, so the measurement is on that base,\n    not on today's origin/main.\n  harness: `python -m rebar.llm.evals.provider_parity --slot <slot> --epochs 3 --concurrency 6`\n  epochs 3 per item per arm, majority decision; corpus 30 enumerated / 28 scored (below);\n  corpus_digest 9d707f762efbaad3bd1190373af1a878c41d801c28f7824c5a532d41eef00c2a\n  case-runs 90 per arm per slot = 360 total; provider requests 377/366 (standard v1/v2) and\n  325/338 (frontier v1/v2); input tokens 4.27M/4.17M and 3.59M/3.38M.\n\nSTANDARD SLOT — FAILED\n  v1 anthropic claude-sonnet-4-6  <->  v2 bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6\n  (a) structured-output validity ......... PASS  v1 1.000  v2 1.000  (floor 0.99, no regression)\n  (b) per-criterion verdict agreement .... PASS  0.964  (floor 0.95)\n  (b) ZERO decision flips on gold ........ FAIL  1 flip  (must be 0)\n  (c) recall ............................. PASS  v1 0.857 -> v2 0.929  (IMPROVED +7.1pp)\n  (c) false-accept ....................... PASS  v1 0.786  v2 0.786  (unchanged)\n  (d) runtime error rate ................. PASS  v1 0.000  v2 0.000  (no regression)\n  (e) gold-coverage guard ................ PASS  n_gold 28 >= 20, min_gold left at its DEFAULT\n  latency (informational, non-gating) .... v1 2756.5s  v2 2484.6s  (Bedrock 9.9% FASTER)\n  gating_failures: [\"1 decision-level flip(s) on the gold set (must be 0)\"]\n\n  THE FLIP: code-review-db-migrations / R-drop-column-no-backfill, gold label BLOCK.\n    v1 advisory (MISSED it)  ->  v2 block (CAUGHT it). Both errored=False, valid=True.\n    The flip is Bedrock being MORE accurate; it is the same event as the recall improvement.\n\nFRONTIER SLOT — FAILED\n  v1 anthropic claude-opus-4-8  <->  v2 bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8\n  (a) structured-output validity ......... PASS  v1 1.000  v2 1.000\n  (b) per-criterion verdict agreement .... FAIL  0.929  (floor 0.95)\n  (b) ZERO decision flips on gold ........ FAIL  2 flips  (must be 0)\n  (c) recall ............................. PASS  v1 0.929  v2 0.929  (unchanged)\n  (c) false-accept ....................... FAIL  v1 0.786 -> v2 0.929, \"rose 0.143 > margin 0.02\"\n  (d) runtime error rate ................. PASS  v1 0.000  v2 0.000\n  (e) gold-coverage guard ................ PASS  n_gold 28 >= 20, min_gold left at its DEFAULT\n  latency (informational, non-gating) .... v1 2103.1s  v2 2105.1s  (within 0.1%)\n  gating_failures: [\"verdict agreement 0.929 below 0.95\",\n                    \"2 decision-level flip(s) on the gold set (must be 0)\",\n                    \"false-accept rose 0.143 > margin 0.02\"]\n\n  THE FLIPS, both gold label ADVISORY, both v1 block -> v2 advisory, all four records\n  errored=False and valid=True:\n    code-review-api-compat   / FP-rename-all-callsites-updated\n    code-review-db-migrations/ FP-create-index-concurrently\n  On both, v1 (direct Anthropic) FALSE-FIRED on a case gold says is clean and v2 (Bedrock) did\n  not. Again the flips are Bedrock being more accurate.\n\n  READ THE FRONTIER false-accept FAILURE WITH CARE — it is very likely an inverted metric, not a\n  Bedrock regression. `parity._recall_false_accept` computes\n  `false_accept = (safe items whose decision != \"block\") / (safe items)`, where \"safe\" is\n  `label != \"block\"`. That is the fraction of clean items CORRECTLY not blocked, i.e. specificity\n  -- higher is BETTER -- yet `parity_report` fails the run when it RISES. So v2 is being failed\n  for false-firing LESS than v1. The 0.143 delta is exactly the 2 flips above (2/14). Filed\n  separately; NOT fixed here (out of scope, and the bar is the bar).\n\nNOT THE 635f ARTIFACT — CHECKED FIRST, AS THE TICKET REQUIRES. Error rate is 0.000 on all four\narms and every flipped pair has errored=False on BOTH sides, so no flip can be a laundered\nerror. Independently, the harness never gives `parity_report` an errored pair at all: errored\nindex pairs are dropped before scoring, precisely because `parity_report` selects gold pairs on\n`a.label` alone and then compares decisions with NO `errored` guard, so an arm that merely\nfailed to run would score as a flip. Mutation-verified: removing that filter turns three tests\nRED, including one asserting a transient throttle is not a flip.\n\nTHE TWO EXCLUDED PAIRS ARE A FIXTURE GAP, NOT A PROVIDER EVENT. plan-review-container's\nG3-R-uncovered-ac-rebar and G3-FP-covered-by-named-consumer-rebar raised\n`ValueError: container criterion 'G3' needs a non-empty children list in the eval fixture` on\nBOTH arms at ALL 3 epochs, before any model call (confirmed: 84 usage rows for 90 case-runs on\nevery arm = exactly 2 items x 3 epochs missing). Provider-independent and zero spend. They are\nnow excluded from the corpus by `_runnable`, so the selector returns the same 28 items that were\nactually scored. Note this hits the plan's own worked example, which assumed\nG3-R-uncovered-ac-rebar would run.\n\nVERDICT: Bedrock does NOT clear the parity bar at either class slot as the bar is written. The\nevidence does NOT show Bedrock is worse — all three flips favour Bedrock on gold accuracy, and\nvalidity, error rate and latency are at or better than parity. But \"zero decision-level flips\"\nis unmet, and this story does not get to reinterpret the bar it was asked to apply.\n"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785716305273731001,"uuid":"b4519995-6c84-45a6-a849-c0b3c281b732"}